  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>Dividend Guide is an independent educational resource about dividend stocks, ETFs, distributions, yield, and long-term income planning. The goal is to explain data clearly, not to provide personalized investment advice.</p>
  <h2>Authorship and Review</h2>
  <p>Articles are written and fact-checked by <a href="/about/author/">Henry Zhou</a>, Independent Dividend Researcher. The site does not use a separate review board unless a named reviewer and profile are shown on the article.</p>
  <h2>Research Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Define the topic, date range, and intended calculation.</li>
    <li>Use primary sources where available, including company filings, fund issuer documents, SEC records, and official index reports.</li>
    <li>Record source URLs, access dates, data cutoff dates, and statistical assumptions.</li>
    <li>Separate reported figures from derived calculations and clearly label estimates.</li>
    <li>Review the article for factual consistency, source accuracy, and financial disclaimers.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Data and Methodology</h2>
  <p>Every data-driven article should state the relevant date range, price date, distribution period, yield definition, split-adjustment treatment, and whether special distributions are included. When a figure is calculated, the formula and inputs should be explained near the figure.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and Updates</h2>
  <p>If you find an error, email <a href="mailto:hello@dividend01.com">hello@dividend01.com</a> with the page URL and supporting source. Material corrections are reflected in the article's updated date and, where useful, in an editorial note.</p>
  <h2>Disclosure</h2>
  <p>Dividend Guide is not a broker, investment adviser, tax adviser, or fund issuer. Content is for education only. Past performance does not guarantee future results, and readers should verify current data and seek qualified advice for their own circumstances.</p>
